From c332e3ef2fb20cab8aa57bef4940892cd81d2e6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:26:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DiscSoftTelecineScan: a scan left in the close of what it
 read with parks when the close comes back

When Kodi closes, CDiscSoftTelecineScan::StopAll() waits 2 s for the scans
of the titles of a disc, and 1 s more for those that close what they read
with (BeginFinish()); a scan still running then is given up
(KODI::DISC::StopAllScans() sets abandoned), and Kodi takes down its
services, the clients of SMB and NFS, the libraries and the log. A scan
given up in a read parks when the read comes back (ParkIfAbandoned() in
the callbacks of the image), but one given up in its finish, in the close
of the navigator or of the image (CFile::Close() of an image on a share of
SMB that went away can take longer than that second), did not: back from
the close, Run() ended, which lets libdvdnav go through Kodi's section
loader (~DllDvdNav) and frees the item that it read (CFileItem), and
RunDetached() destroyed what the job held, all of it after Kodi was gone.

The finish of Run() now parks once the closes are done where the scan was
given up meanwhile, as a read that comes back does. Where nothing was
given up (every scan ended in time, or Kodi is not closing) nothing
changes.

Tests (outside the tree): longclose_wiring.py, the finish of Run() in the
tree (2 of its checks fail before this change); t_longclose.cpp, the
registry of the tree with a job in the order of Run() whose close takes
900 ms against a shutdown that waits 300 + 200 ms: without the park after
the close the scan touches Kodi after the shutdown, with it, not. The
t_scanexit cases of the registry (none, hung, busy, finishing, closed)
pass, and their three mutants fail as before.
---
 .../VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DiscSoftTelecineScan.cpp     | 5 ++++-
 .../cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DiscSoftTelecineScan.h | 5 +++--
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DiscSoftTelecineScan.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DiscSoftTelecineScan.cpp
index cfc80b1..527cb06 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DiscSoftTelecineScan.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DiscSoftTelecineScan.cpp
@@ -212,7 +212,9 @@ void CDiscSoftTelecineScan::Run(const CFileItem& item,
   callbacks.pf_seek = cbSeek;
 
   // (where Kodi, closing, gave the scan up meanwhile, it parks here: nothing that it read with is
-  // closed, KODI::DISC::BeginFinish())
+  // closed, KODI::DISC::BeginFinish(); and where it gave the scan up while it closed them, a close
+  // that did not come back in time, it parks once they are: what is left to do then, the library
+  // let go and the item it read freed, is Kodi's)
   const auto finish = [&]
   {
     KODI::DISC::BeginFinish();
@@ -220,6 +222,7 @@ void CDiscSoftTelecineScan::Run(const CFileItem& item,
       dll.dvdnav_close(nav);
     if (image)
       image->file.Close();
+    KODI::DISC::ParkIfAbandoned();
   };
 
   if (!dll.Load())
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DiscSoftTelecineScan.h b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DiscSoftTelecineScan.h
index 25e223d..a1fe438 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DiscSoftTelecineScan.h
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DiscSoftTelecineScan.h
@@ -49,8 +49,9 @@ public:
    * \brief Kodi closes (CApplication::Stop(), before the clients of SMB and NFS, the libraries and
    *        the log go away): every scan stops and none starts; those that run are waited for up to
    *        2 s, and those closing what they read with up to 1 s more. One still in a read of the
-   *        disc that does not come back is left, and parks for good when it does: it touches
-   *        nothing of Kodi from then on (KODI::DISC::StopAllScans()). Where no scan runs, at once.
+   *        disc, or in the close of what it read with, that does not come back is left, and parks
+   *        for good when it does: it touches nothing of Kodi from then on
+   *        (KODI::DISC::StopAllScans()). Where no scan runs, at once.
    */
   static void StopAll();
 
